/E (To create a calculated column in Power BI to show the profit margin percentage, follow these steps: 1. Go to the Data view in Power BI Desktop. 2. Select the table where you want to create the new column. 3. Click on the New Column button in the Modeling tab. 4. Enter the formula for the calculated column. For example: Profit Margin = \(Sales - Cost\) / Sales * 100 5. Press Enter. This will create a new column in your table showing the profit margin percentage for each row. )
